      "reasons": [
        "The definition’s first sentence (“Concurrent validity is the extent to which a measure shows the expected relationship with another relevant measure assessed at the same time.”) is not stated or explicitly supported anywhere in the provided packet text.",
        "The packet only provides an example of concurrent validity for TAPAS (correlation with weight stigma, r = 0.49) and does not supply the general “extent/expected relationship” wording requested in the definition.",
